WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:03.700
I fought every rune bear in Elden ring
so that you don't have to.

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:05.800
There were 21 in total.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.833
It was awful,
but one of them was worth killing.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
And two of them were actually very unique.

00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:15.666
See, everyone who plays Elden Ring
fights these things once or twice

00:00:15.666 --> 00:00:18.666
and then just ignores them
for the rest of their playthrough.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:19.800
Rightfully so.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.433
Most of them just look like the one
I'm fighting now.

00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:24.666
Some of them have an absurd
amount of health.

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:27.966
Some are covered in snow,
some are asleep, some weight, an ambush.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.066
But overall their movesets and behavior
are largely the same,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.500
except for one found here
south of the deep XI for a well in colored

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.633
and one found here southeast of the inner
consecrated snow field.

00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:44.866
These two have ragged unkempt fur,

00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:48.500
which I think suggests
that they're more feral than the others.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.733
And it shows because their moveset
has all of the usual B.S.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.000
but it also includes a skyward dive attack
and an AOP roar.

00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:02.333
Not only that, but their health
and defense is just through the roof,

00:01:02.566 --> 00:01:07.666
especially this one in the snow field,
which is basically an end game field boss.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:12.200
It also just happens to be the only bloody
run bear that's actually worth killing.

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:16.033
You can find it here
buried in the snow as a wandering noble.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.700
It's actually mimicked here.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.933
And if you somehow overcome it,
you'll receive a larval tier,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.966
which you can use to respec
your character.

00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:26.933
Number two, while in Caleb.

00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:31.366
Did you ever notice these piles of weapons
that litter its battlefields?

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:34.666
These, I think, help to convey the sheer

00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:38.066
scale of the battle
where millennia fought to retain.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:41.633
And they're mostly found
in these sections of Caleb

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.500
here, where millennia experienced her
first scarlet bloom, and here near Red

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:52.400
Main Castle in the arena that I believe
Rodan fled to after succumbing to the rot.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.133
We talked really in-depth about Caleb's
lore in this video,

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:59.733
and it's obvious in retrospect,
but a lot of you guys pointed out

00:01:59.733 --> 00:02:03.600
that they're actually curved great swords
among this pile of weapons,

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.466
and they look almost identical
to Riordan's Starsky

00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:11.033
edged Great Swords,
suggesting that some of his soldiers

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:14.033
actually wielded
similar swords to their Lord.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.800
Even though we don't find any soldiers
wielding them in game.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.766
Another curious thing about Riordan's
swords is the inscription

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:25.466
they bear,
which is fittingly the same symbol

00:02:25.466 --> 00:02:29.233
that gravity spells have the swords
actually reference this, stating

00:02:29.233 --> 00:02:34.100
that Broden earned considerable renown
as the star scourge in his youth,

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:38.100
and it is said that it was during
this time that he engraved

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.500
the gravity crest upon these blades.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.266
But what's really cool is that
this gravity crest is likely inspired

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:49.733
by real world models of magnetic forces,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.400
which mark North and South magnetic poles.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.566
These curved lines are likely
the resulting field lines

00:02:57.566 --> 00:03:01.633
that measure the strength
and direction of magnetic fields,

00:03:01.633 --> 00:03:06.300
which results in a graph
that looks a lot like the gravity crest.

00:03:06.366 --> 00:03:10.066
Considering gravity spells
do pertain to the push

00:03:10.066 --> 00:03:15.200
and pull of cosmic forces,
I can see the connection though.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.966
Diving any deeper into this topic
makes my brain hurt, so I'll stop here.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:25.100
Rodan initially learned this gravity magic
so that he could ride his scrawny horse.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.833
Despite his immense size.

00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:30.000
Then he furthered his knowledge
in order to confront

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.700
the falling stars
and seal the fate in the night sky.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.633
So naturally, Rodan displays
this incredible mastery over gravity magic

00:03:38.633 --> 00:03:42.766
in our fight with him, even
managing to manifest as a giant meteor

00:03:42.766 --> 00:03:45.766
and devastate anything in his path.

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:50.733
But the big thing when missing from Rodan
story is why he went this far.

00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:53.466
Why did he have to conquer the stars?

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:57.400
And to be honest, I've always felt like
we're missing something from this topic.

00:03:57.633 --> 00:04:01.200
Take, for example,
the sword gravestone in Celaya.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.966
It states that Rodan alone
holds CLIA secure.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.500
Then consider these stars good heirloom.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.500
It states that Rodan confronted
the falling stars.

00:04:11.566 --> 00:04:15.300
It almost sounds
as if the stars were a threat in some way.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.066
Right.

00:04:16.066 --> 00:04:20.566
As if Rodan was taking defensive measures
in conquering the stars

00:04:20.666 --> 00:04:23.833
rather than taking the offensive
initiative.

00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:27.500
And there's a piece of cut content
that might just

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.333
explain
why the story is presented this way.

00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:34.700
So in one of his
all these videos, she presents evidence

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.866
that a still the malformed star

00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:41.700
boss might have actually been
a part of your fight with Rodan.

00:04:41.966 --> 00:04:45.866
This is because I still actually
has a cut animation that shows them

00:04:45.866 --> 00:04:49.066
descending from the sky,
covering this enormous amount

00:04:49.066 --> 00:04:52.266
of distance in the process
and crashing to the ground

00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:57.000
with the same fiery VFX
that Rodan himself uses.

00:04:57.066 --> 00:05:00.900
And while the fiery VFX is missing
from this descent,

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:04.833
Zoglin notes that the animation does
include fiery sound effects,

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.366
making the meteor comparison
even more valid.

00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:12.166
So imagine you've just defeated
Riordan's first phase

00:05:12.166 --> 00:05:16.500
and he disappears from the arena demigod,
defeated, Right.

00:05:16.566 --> 00:05:18.266
The stars are free.

00:05:18.266 --> 00:05:23.033
Suddenly a fiery meteor comes
rushing towards you, narrowly misses

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:28.666
and then unfolds to reveal Esto phase
two of Riordan's fight.

00:05:28.766 --> 00:05:34.033
And the very thing that Riordan himself
was holding back from the world.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.433
That's how I imagine it playing out.

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:40.166
At least it would have really driven home
the idea that Rodan

00:05:40.166 --> 00:05:44.600
was preventing these falling star beasts
from making planet for.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.066
And it's a really compelling theory
as to why Riordan

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.066
might have acted
as the star coach in the first place.

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:57.500
Now, obviously it's cut content
and it can't really be considered canon,

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.166
and I personally think that Riordan's
motivations can still be more complex

00:06:02.166 --> 00:06:05.533
than just being limited
to this defensive action.

00:06:05.533 --> 00:06:10.300
But perhaps this explains
why the law is so vague on this topic,

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.866
almost as if the obvious explanation
was removed from the game.

00:06:15.933 --> 00:06:18.933
But speaking of Rodan and his wars,

00:06:18.966 --> 00:06:21.966
so this character is the Knight Jarrin,

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:25.900
who served as a commander
in General Riordan's Wars.

00:06:25.966 --> 00:06:31.500
And he has this very curious line
of dialog to say about e.g.

00:06:31.566 --> 00:06:35.733
who was the blacksmith
for the Carrion royal family.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.500
Bit of a haughty sort.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.033
Strange fellow when I knew him.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:45.700
And funny thing is
swords were all blood to stone,

00:06:45.766 --> 00:06:49.866
but not one of them decayed
when faced with the scarlet rot.

00:06:49.933 --> 00:06:53.333
We learn three fascinating things
from this dialog.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.933
First, the e.g.

00:06:54.933 --> 00:06:59.166
Carrion Royal Blacksmith actually
made weapons for some of Riordan's forces

00:06:59.166 --> 00:07:02.366
who eventually came into contact
with the scarlet rot.

00:07:02.466 --> 00:07:05.800
Second, we learned that
not one of these weapons decayed.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.800
That's quite the achievement, as scarlet

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.800
rot is an incredibly corrosive force.

00:07:11.866 --> 00:07:13.300
Even Melania's Knights

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:17.000
needed to have their weapons
consecrated in order to ward it off.

00:07:17.233 --> 00:07:22.433
The only downside of these weapons is that
apparently they were blunt as stone.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.166
Seems odd that they'd be used at all.

00:07:25.166 --> 00:07:28.466
But I guess we just have
to take that quote at face value.

00:07:28.666 --> 00:07:31.666
What's very interesting
here, though, is that next to e.g.,

00:07:31.666 --> 00:07:35.866
we can actually see a greatsword,
which is a weapon that you can actually

00:07:35.866 --> 00:07:37.200
loot for yourself in.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.100
Caleb suggesting
that it might have been one of his weapons

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.133
that made it all the way there.

00:07:43.133 --> 00:07:46.966
Not only that, but the Great Sword
is actually a recurring reference

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:50.700
placed in many of Fromsoftware games,
and it's this homage

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:54.233
to the Great Sword
that's wielded by guts from Berserk.

00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:57.700
A weapon that is, and I quote, massive,

00:07:57.833 --> 00:08:00.800
thick, heavy and far too rough.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.400
It was much too big to be called a sword.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.300
Indeed, it was like a heap of raw iron.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:10.966
So I wonder, are these great swords
what Jaron is referring to

00:08:11.166 --> 00:08:14.100
when he talks about his blunt weapons?

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.733
Maybe so.

