00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:16.000
But let's get back to it.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.833
For number six,
the Leonia maps all read as follows.

00:09:20.933 --> 00:09:24.566
The majority of Leonia, known
for its vast forests

00:09:24.566 --> 00:09:28.666
and ever
present fog, is sinking into a lake.

00:09:28.766 --> 00:09:31.933
But why is it sinking into the lake?

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:36.166
The map says that it was known
for its vast forests and ever present fog,

00:09:36.166 --> 00:09:40.166
but it doesn't say that it was known
for its marshes or swampland.

00:09:40.166 --> 00:09:43.166
So surely it wasn't always like this.

00:09:43.233 --> 00:09:48.033
What's more, did the order of real lucario
with all of their collective intellect

00:09:48.033 --> 00:09:53.033
really think to build their academy
and surrounding town on a swamp?

00:09:53.233 --> 00:09:55.733
Is it possible
they were that shortsighted?

00:09:55.733 --> 00:09:56.933
I don't think so.

00:09:56.933 --> 00:10:01.733
And as for why the land is sinking,
I feel like there might be two options.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:05.400
Either this environmental change
could have been sudden

00:10:05.466 --> 00:10:09.100
and caused by the shattering with water
maybe

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.100
spewing down from the north,
from the Altus plateau.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:15.233
Or maybe the place was always watery.

00:10:15.233 --> 00:10:21.333
But perhaps something else
has caused the land to soften from below.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.433
So take a look at your map
and you'll notice

00:10:23.433 --> 00:10:27.100
that the lake of rot
is actually directly below Leonia.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.033
What's more,
if you look up from the lake of rot,

00:10:30.033 --> 00:10:34.166
you can actually see a giant limestone
crystal peeking through the roof,

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:37.200
which I think confirms
that Fromsoftware did in fact

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.866
consider the upper and lower
alignment of these two places.

00:10:42.033 --> 00:10:46.433
The Academy relies upon this glint stone
that they built

00:10:46.433 --> 00:10:50.166
their entire academy on top of
so in order to claim it,

00:10:50.166 --> 00:10:55.300
maybe they simply looked past lands,
poor foundations or something like that.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.666
But anyway, the lake of rot is seething.

00:10:57.666 --> 00:11:01.466
It's constantly steaming
and filling the air with its pollution.

00:11:01.466 --> 00:11:06.400
So I feel like it's a fair theory
to think that this could have slowly

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:12.566
eroded the land above over time, causing
Leonia to maybe sink into the lake.

00:11:12.633 --> 00:11:14.133
Special thanks to Kellogg

00:11:14.133 --> 00:11:18.200
linked in the description
