00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:24.400
Speaking of environmental analysis,
two months ago, someone on Reddit

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:29.233
discovered these reliefs etched on
two pillars at Nicholas Haley's tree.

00:11:29.266 --> 00:11:32.400
They then attempted to extrapolate
meaning from them.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.466
Fair enough.

00:11:33.466 --> 00:11:37.800
The floral design at the lower end,
they claimed, depicted Melania's

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:42.400
first second and third blooms
from which the root goddess emerged.

00:11:42.466 --> 00:11:48.000
Continuing up, we see an enclosed owl
supposedly representing sublime slumber

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.833
enjoyed by Mikala,
who is in the womb, only to emerge

00:11:51.833 --> 00:11:56.200
in this elder state, having quelled
the curse of eternal childhood.

00:11:56.433 --> 00:12:00.233
So this post received over 2000 updates,

00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:04.733
and a lot of people
clearly took a liking to the theory

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:08.366
until someone pointed out
that these pillars

00:12:08.433 --> 00:12:12.566
are also found in path of Exile
a different game,

00:12:12.633 --> 00:12:18.066
meaning that path of Exile and Elden Ring
clearly exist within the same universe.

00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:21.166
Or that Fromsoftware
bought this asset from a public asset

00:12:21.166 --> 00:12:24.166
library in order to save time and money.

00:12:24.166 --> 00:12:26.666
You know, it's
probably that second one, actually.

00:12:26.666 --> 00:12:30.466
I like that someone in the comments claims
that this situation came about

00:12:30.466 --> 00:12:33.466
because of Epifanio,
which was a good word to learn,

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:38.100
because it is a word
that refers to the tendency to perceive

00:12:38.133 --> 00:12:42.733
a connection or meaningful pattern
between unrelated or random things.

00:12:42.966 --> 00:12:47.966
And it's so easy to be guilty of this
when analyzing from software's lore,

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.966
you'll come up with a theory,
and before long you're looking for

00:12:50.966 --> 00:12:54.233
any evidence that proves your theory
and strokes your ego

00:12:54.266 --> 00:12:58.366
rather than looking at all of the evidence
objectively as you should.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:02.266
It reminds me of this video
I made a while back where I argued that

00:13:02.266 --> 00:13:06.700
all of the Souls board games
were canonically connected to each other

00:13:06.766 --> 00:13:11.233
as in all their stories bled into one
another and told one big story.

00:13:11.233 --> 00:13:16.133
And in that video I was really clear
that that video was just for fun

00:13:16.333 --> 00:13:19.500
and I was very clear
that I was purposefully cherry

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:22.900
picking arguments
in order to support my theories.

00:13:22.933 --> 00:13:27.833
And yet still a lot of people
in the comments bought into the idea

00:13:27.833 --> 00:13:31.366
and started to actually believe
that the games were connected.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:35.266
So that video now serves
as a very good example.

00:13:35.366 --> 00:13:40.133
A warning that it is very easy
to be misled by someone

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.300
if they're speaking with confidence

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:45.800
on a topic
that you are not completely familiar with.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:47.933
Anyway, back to the reliefs.

00:13:47.933 --> 00:13:52.600
I'm not saying that all architectural
analysis of Elden Ring is invalid.

00:13:52.666 --> 00:13:54.500
It's not a lot of Elden rings.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:58.866
Architecture is probably handcrafted
with intent and you could even argue

00:13:58.866 --> 00:14:02.733
that the public assets
that Fromsoftware do use were chosen

00:14:02.966 --> 00:14:06.266
because they align perfectly
with Elden Ring's lore.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.900
But I do think it's naive to think
that every single thing

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:13.266
in Fromsoftware
games are handcrafted with intent.

00:14:13.266 --> 00:14:19.000
And I do think it's important to remember
how easy it is to be misled.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:24.700
Speaking of which, this next secret also
deserves a healthy dose of skepticism.

00:14:24.766 --> 00:14:26.966
So as they were fighting Godric.

00:14:26.966 --> 00:14:31.633
User Jack Newby 555 noticed
that while Godric is right

00:14:31.633 --> 00:14:35.366
leg is a mass of flesh,
his left leg is armored,

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:40.633
and it's this left leg that Godric uses
to summon storm winds for his attacks.

00:14:40.833 --> 00:14:46.200
Most importantly, they argue that this leg
looks suspiciously similar to Commander

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:51.233
Nyle, someone who summon storms
with a stamp of their foot as well.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:56.166
So how likely is it
really that Godric took Nigel's leg

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:58.900
and bolted it onto his own body?

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:01.366
Well, unlike the previous secret,
I actually think

00:15:01.366 --> 00:15:04.366
this one has a lot of merit.
Let me explain.

00:15:04.466 --> 00:15:07.966
So, Commander
Nigel is a veteran general of Seoul,

00:15:08.033 --> 00:15:13.666
a lone survivor who commanded spirits
to defend his long past master.

00:15:13.766 --> 00:15:15.400
But apart from that description,

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.233
we actually know very little about him
and his allegiances.

00:15:19.233 --> 00:15:23.366
And the same goes for Commander O'Neill,
who is another veteran

00:15:23.366 --> 00:15:25.166
boss of similar design.

00:15:25.166 --> 00:15:30.100
But what's relevant to us here is Niall's
prosthetic leg and its description,

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:34.733
which reads Bladed prosthetic leg
and wreathed with the power of lightning.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:39.333
Commander Nigel, veteran of Castle
Seoul, offered this prosthesis

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:43.166
in exchange for the lives of defeated
knights held prisoner.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:46.666
As I was reading this,
something immediately stuck out to me.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:50.333
Why does it say that
Nigel offered this prosthesis?

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:51.433
That doesn't make sense.

00:15:51.433 --> 00:15:56.700
How could he have offered up a prosthetic
leg that he actually uses in his fight?

00:15:56.933 --> 00:16:02.200
So I went to our trusty translator, Loki,
who reveals that the Japanese text

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.700
actually just says that leg,
meaning the true description,

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:11.633
is probably more like Commander
Nigel offered his leg in exchange

00:16:11.633 --> 00:16:16.566
for the lives of defeated knights
held prisoner Godric and Godfrey.

00:16:16.566 --> 00:16:20.066
Two, for that matter,
are the only major players in the Elden

00:16:20.066 --> 00:16:23.566
ring that I can think of
who would actually be happy

00:16:23.566 --> 00:16:27.133
to receive the offering of a leg
as payment for something.

00:16:27.333 --> 00:16:31.666
And Niall
and O'Neil are both missing legs,

00:16:31.766 --> 00:16:36.833
which could explain both Godric
and goto Freud's possession of them.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:41.100
So I think it's a great theory
that could easily have been a situation

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:45.166
where Godric or Godfrey held Niles Knights
prisoner,

00:16:45.233 --> 00:16:50.200
leading to the offering of a powerful limb
in exchange for their safe return.

00:16:50.266 --> 00:16:54.200
The best counter evidence to this theory,
though, is that Godric and Godfrey

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:58.200
are actually using right legs
as left legs here.

00:16:58.266 --> 00:17:01.733
But as pointed out by some others
in the comments,

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:06.400
this probably wasn't a deal breaker
for Godfrey or Godfrey.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.266
And at the very least,
if you don't like this theory,

00:17:09.266 --> 00:17:14.266
I think that this could easily
be the leg of any banished knight as well,

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:17.866
who were a class of warriors
who mastered storms

00:17:17.866 --> 00:17:22.933
and who could have passed that mastery
over to the grafted.

00:17:23.033 --> 00:17:27.300
Of all the characters in Elden Ring,
Roderick is the one who was the most

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:31.600
personally affected by the grafting,
for she ventured to the lands

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:36.866
between from across the sea,
only to barely escape with her own life.

00:17:36.933 --> 00:17:39.933
Everyone's been grafted.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:44.033
Everyone who came with me,
they crossed the sea for me.

00:17:44.066 --> 00:17:48.033
They fought for me

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:51.400
only to have their arms taken,

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:56.800
their legs taken, even their heads taken,

00:17:56.866 --> 00:18:00.700
Taken and stuck to the spider.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:04.333
According to her crimson hood,
Roderick is expatriated

00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:08.066
